WEBVTT

00:00.700 --> 00:03.775
Every product has a story. Most catalogs show a

00:03.787 --> 00:07.741
still image. Meet SKU to Scene: AI-directed
video for

00:07.753 --> 00:11.816
retail and consumer goods, powered by Copilot
agents and

00:11.852 --> 00:12.958
Microsoft Foundry.

00:14.933 --> 00:21.470
Seasonal launches. Product pages. Social
campaigns. In-store screens. Start

00:21.482 --> 00:24.883
with approved product imagery and a
merchandising brief, then

00:24.895 --> 00:27.191
explore creative shaped for each channel.

00:29.167 --> 00:32.662
Three specialist agents work as a Squad. The
merchandiser

00:32.674 --> 00:35.595
shapes the scene. The router selects a model and

00:35.607 --> 00:39.189
applies budget guardrails. Brand QA screens the
result.

00:41.133 --> 00:46.037
For quick-service restaurants, coffee, and
convenience retail, bring limited-time

00:46.133 --> 00:50.567
offers into focus. Compare fast-tier concepts,
choose a direction,

00:50.819 --> 00:52.922
and explore a separate hero render.

00:54.883 --> 00:58.513
Image-to-video brings the approved product into
a seasonal story.

00:58.860 --> 01:03.115
Here, visual screening passed, but mismatched
native audio blocked

01:03.127 --> 01:06.312
publication. That audio is muted in this
showcase.

01:08.267 --> 01:11.620
For apparel and lifestyle commerce, give the
lookbook life.

01:11.967 --> 01:15.621
Explore fabric movement and camera motion from
the catalog

01:15.633 --> 01:18.673
image, with product identity as the reference.

01:20.617 --> 01:24.631
For home improvement and electronics, help
shoppers imagine products

01:24.643 --> 01:30.434
in context: demonstrations, project inspiration,
and multi-object scenes. Unmet

01:30.446 --> 01:32.394
requirements stay visible for rework.

01:34.367 --> 01:39.391
For grocery, pharmacy, and consumer goods,
explore weekly circulars,

01:39.703 --> 01:44.545
digital endcaps, and seasonal campaigns. Fast
models support iteration;

01:44.942 --> 01:47.670
fidelity checks flag concepts needing rework.

01:49.633 --> 01:53.622
Five fal variants offer different creative
strengths. Routing considers

01:53.634 --> 01:58.706
source assets, speed, budget, and audio
requirements. Preview cost

01:58.718 --> 02:00.677
estimates remain separate from bills.

02:02.633 --> 02:06.153
Open the browser demo without an Azure
deployment. Replay

02:06.165 --> 02:10.276
authentic recorded renders, inspect routing, and
explore the evidence.

02:10.624 --> 02:12.018
Nothing new is generated.

02:13.983 --> 02:18.056
Two clips passed automated screening; six
failed. Every clip

02:18.080 --> 02:22.936
requires human sign-off. Foundry evaluations add
context without replacing

02:22.948 --> 02:24.005
original verdicts.

02:25.950 --> 02:29.938
Live generation is optional and billable.
Preview processing runs

02:29.950 --> 02:34.710
outside Microsoft facilities under fal's terms.
Microsoft customer agreements,

02:34.987 --> 02:39.193
the Product Terms, DPA, and certifications do
not apply.

02:41.167 --> 02:44.963
Start with one product category and one channel.
Explore

02:44.975 --> 02:49.326
the demo. Inspect the evidence. Shape your
pilot. SKU

02:49.338 --> 02:52.246
to Scene. From product image to possibility.
